 ],
 "notes": "Things to check: (1) Portland Low (1008-1010, 1403): Portland Bill had two lights then, but stations.json has only one portland-bill id. Consider adding a Portland Low id. (2) Plain 'Holyhead' (594, 1391) is mapped to holyhead-breakwater, but South Stack or the town are possible. (3) Falmouth (378) is a place, but it could be St Anthony Head ('Falmouth Harbour L.H.'). (4) Caldy Island (198) and St Tudwal's Island (192) are mapped to their lighthouses; they become places if the observers were not keepers. (5) 'Baytor Mere, Devon' (116) is unidentified; check the page image. (6) 'Grimsdale' (515) is assumed to be Grinsdale. (7) Burgh (184) is assumed to be Burgh by Sands. (8) Gretna (511) is in Scotland despite being filed under Cumberland. (9) 'Wolf Rock L.V.' (1418) and 'Godrevy L.v.' (485) are treated as type errors for the lighthouses. (10) 'St Ann's High' (1191) is mapped to the 1884+ single row st-anns-head. (11) 'S.W. stations' (1064) is marked none; set the station list yourself if wanted. (12) Calf of Man (203) is a place; it is chicken-rock if it comes from that return. (13) Allonby 1886 (55) is a place, because the Allonby station is listed only in 1881. (14) All Nash variants map to nash-point-high, the only Nash light listed after 1881.",
